---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
---

<Layout title="About | Ursa fab.">
  <Header alwaysVisible />

  <main class="content-page">
    <section class="content-media">
      <div class="content-hero">
        <img src="/about.jpeg" alt="Ursa fab. workshop" />
      </div>

      <p class="content-label-about"><b>THE CRAFTING BEAR</b> - <em>Ursus fabricatoris f. difficilis</em></p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-copy">
      <h1>Bespoke fabrication, designed and built in Norwich.</h1>

      <p>
        Existing at the juncture between garage industry and large-scale fabrication, 
        we aim to make high-end metalcraft as accessible as possible to artists, 
        creatives, homes, and small businesses. 
        Whether you have a fully-fledged  design, a sketch of an idea, or just a 
        problem to solve, we can make your projects a reality in almost any metal - 
        using the best possible manual welding and machining equipment, precision 
        fixturing, in-house design and selected materials partners.
      </p>
      <br/>
      <br/>
      <hr/>
      <br/>

      <p>
        Ursa fab. is the professional expression of myself, Tom van Baalen - 
        a resident of Norwich since 2008, studying at the University of East Anglia. 
        Grown from a love of handcrafts, heritage industry, and the world both 
        beyond and behind us; it is, I hope, a vehicle to make long-lasting and 
        beautiful things for the people that appreciate them.
      </p>

      <p>
      As the need became overwhelming - to work with my hands and make - I took 
      an opportunity to leave my past life, in fields and laboratories as a technician, 
      to retrain as a metalworker, and I have been incredibly lucky to learn from some 
      extraordinary colleagues and friends. From a crash course in the fundamentals of 
      materials prep, design, machining, welding and finishing in the workshop of Sam Fish 
      (an enormously skilled and patient craftsperson to whom I am forever indebted), 
      I dove into the deep end of the welding and fabrication industry. Primarily working 
      on sports car subframes and fuel tanks, and further honing my stainless steel welding 
      fabricating hygenic fixtures and fittings, I now follow my own path to make things 
      that are, I hope, interesting, creative and wanted.
      </p>

    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
